## Exhortation to Unity and Humility
 v01 If then there is any encouragement in Christ, any consolation from love, any sharing in the Spirit, any compassion and mercy,
 v02 make my joy complete: be of the same mind, having the same love, being in full accord and of one mind.
 v03 Do nothing from selfish ambition or conceit, but in humility regard others as better than yourselves.
 v04 Let each of you look not to your own interests, but to the interests of others.

## The Mind of Christ
 v05 Let the same mind be in you that was in Christ Jesus,
 v06 who, though he was in the form of God, did not regard equality with God as something to be exploited,
 v07 but emptied himself, taking the form of a servant, being born in human likeness.
 v08 And being found in human form, he humbled himself and became obedient to the point of death—even death on a cross.
 v09 Therefore God highly exalted him and gave him the name that is above every name,
 v10 so that at the name of Jesus every knee should bend, in heaven and on earth and under the earth,
 v11 and every tongue should confess that Jesus Christ is Lord, to the glory of God the Father.

## Living as Children of God
 v12 Therefore, my beloved, just as you have always obeyed, not only in my presence, but now much more in my absence, work out your own salvation with fear and trembling;
 v13 for it is God who is at work in you, enabling you both to will and to work for his good pleasure.
 v14 Do all things without murmuring and arguing,
 v15 so that you may be blameless and innocent, children of God without blemish in the midst of a crooked and perverse generation, among whom you shine like lights in the world,
 v16 holding fast to the word of life, so that on the day of Christ I may boast that I did not run in vain or labor in vain.

## Paul’s Joy and Sacrifice
 v17 But even if I am being poured out as a libation upon the sacrifice and service of your faith, I rejoice and rejoice with all of you;
 v18 and in the same way you also should rejoice and rejoice with me.

## Timothy Commended
 v19 I hope in the Lord Jesus to send Timothy to you soon, so that I too may be encouraged by news of you.
 v20 For I have no one like him, who will be genuinely concerned for your welfare.
 v21 All of them seek their own interests, not the interests of Jesus Christ.
 v22 But you know Timothy’s proven worth, how like a child serving a parent he has served with me in the work of the gospel.
 v23 I hope therefore to send him just as soon as I see how things go with me;
 v24 and I trust in the Lord that I myself will come soon.


## Epaphroditus Commended
 v25 Still, I think it necessary to send to you Epaphroditus—my brother and coworker and fellow soldier, your messenger and minister to my need—
 v26 for he has been longing for all of you and has been distressed because you heard that he was ill.
 v27 Indeed he was ill, and near to death. But God had mercy on him, and not only on him but also on me, so that I would not have sorrow upon sorrow.
 v28 I am all the more eager to send him, therefore, so that you may rejoice at seeing him again, and that I may be less anxious.
 v29 Welcome him then in the Lord with all joy, and honor such people,
 v30 because he came close to death for the work of Christ, risking his life to complete what was lacking in your service to me.

